{"ts": "2026-10-28T22:05:17.324821Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T2156Z-19b4", "unit": "openspec:add-oidc-login", "seq": 49, "type": "task.started", "task": "4.2", "title": "4.2 Write `src/identity/oidc/id-token.test.ts` first (tokens from `fake.mintToken`, `keyFor` from a `createOidcClient`; a `generateKeyPairSync` key signs the hand-made tokens of \"Claim edges\"; each rejection is `await assert.rejects(p, { name: \"OidcError\", code: \"OIDC_TOKEN_INVALID\" })` plus `details.reason`; scenarios \"A valid token\", \"Each flaw is refused\" and \"Claim edges\"), then implement `verifyIdToken` in `src/identity/oidc/id-token.ts`: three base64url parts with JSON header and payload (`malformed`); header `alg` exactly `RS256` and a string `kid` (`alg`); `keyFor(kid)` not `null` (`kid`); `crypto.verify(\"sha256\", ..., createPublicKey({ key: jwk, format: \"jwk\" }), signature)` (`signature`); `iss` equal to `config.issuer` (`issuer`); `aud` the client id or an array holding it (`audience`); `azp` equal to the client id when present, required when `aud` has several entries (`azp`); numeric `exp` with `now < exp + 60 s` (`expired`); numeric `iat` with `iat <= now + 60 s` (`iat`); `nonce` equal in constant time (`nonce`); `sub` of 1 to 512 characters (`subject`); the message is always `invalid ID token`; the result holds the raw `organization` and string-only optional values, implementing requirement \"The ID token is verified before it is trusted\""}
